<title>USA: ComEd says Ill. nuke to be down only 58 days.</title>
<headline>ComEd says Ill. nuke to be down only 58 days.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commonwealth Edison Co (ComEd) said Thursday a refueling outage at its Quad Cities 2 nuclear power station, to begin March 1, will last only 58 days.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a 58-day outage, starting March 1. It'll be back in early May,&quot; said company spokesman Gary Wald.</p>
<p>The company said earlier Thursday the outage would keep the plant off line until the end of June.</p>
<p>The unit, rated at 789 megawatts, is in Cordova, Ill.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk + 212 859 1621))</p>
